    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0404" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11547: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="34" xml:id="d484-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-09T19:55:00+08:00">December 9, 1937—7:55
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 9—11:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0009. Japanese have occupied Chinkiang, surrounded Nanking, advanced within 2
                    miles Wuhu. State will capture Nanking within 24 hours. In order avoid
                    responsibility future damage foreign ships in Yangtze, Japanese issued warning
                    keep clear vicinity Chinese military establishments, if possible leave zone
                    hostilities. <hi rendition="#italic">Idzumo</hi> fired several rounds at 1747.
                    No Chinese planes sighted. Conditions Settlement unchanged.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
